                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Austin/San Antonio TX",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 8 at 5:13PM CST until November 8 at 8:00PM CST by NWS Austin/San Antonio TX",
                "description": "At 513 PM CST, emergency management reported flooding across the\nwarned area with several roads flooded, including around US highway\n377, from Erwin Draw. Areas near Kickapoo Cavern State Park and\nDevils River Natural Area - Del Norte from Dolan Creek have flooding\nas well. Between 2 and 5 inches of rain have fallen over the past 24\nto 36 hours. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in\nthe warned area.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Recent rains producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, along\nhighways where low water crossings exist.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nRocksprings, Loma Alta, Carta Valley, Vinegarone, Kickapoo Cavern\nState Park, Devils River State Nat Area Del Norte, Devil's Sinkhole\nState Natural Area, Devils River State Nat Area Big Satan, Devils\nShores and Pafford Crossing.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nIn hilly terrain there are hundreds of low water crossings which are\npotentially dangerous in heavy rain. Do not attempt to cross flooded\nroads. Find an alternate route.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.",
                "response": "Avoid",
